  "question": "In British Columbia, Alberta, Ontario and Quebec, did the tree cover lost between 1984 and 2022 come back?",
  "answer": "Across the four provinces 55,132,072 ha of land was treed in one year and not the next. 36.7 percent of it was treed again for at least three consecutive years after its most recent loss, and 40.6 percent after any loss. 46,424,718 ha is Unknown because at least one year is unclassified or missing, and is excluded, not counted as zero. Treed means VLCE2 classes 210, 220 and 230 only. This measures return of tree cover, not return of the forest that was there, and it is not NFI forest.",
